    "2️⃣ OYLAR (12 TA)\n\n📌 QISH (Winter):\n  • December — dekabr\n  • January — yanvar\n  • February — fevral\n\n📌 BAHOR (Spring):\n  • March — mart\n  • April — aprel\n  • May — may\n\n📌 YOZ (Summer):\n  • June — iyun\n  • July — iyul\n  • August — avgust\n\n📌 KUZ (Autumn/Fall):\n  • September — sentyabr\n  • October — oktyabr\n  • November — noyabr\n\n📌 'In' bilan:\n  in January — yanvar oyida\n  in July — iyul oyida\n  I was born in March. (Men martda tug'ilganman)",
    "3️⃣ FASLLAR (4 TA)\n\n📌 BAHOR (Spring):\n  March, April, May — gullar ochiladi\n\n📌 YOZ (Summer):\n  June, July, August — issiq, ta'til\n\n📌 KUZ (Autumn / Fall — AmE):\n  September, October, November — barglar to'kiladi\n\n📌 QISH (Winter):\n  December, January, February — sovuq, qor\n\n📌 'In' bilan:\n  in spring — bahorda\n  in summer — yozda\n  in autumn — kuzda\n  in winter — qishda",
    "4️⃣ 'ON', 'IN', 'AT' — VAQT PREDLOGLARI\n\n📌 ON + kunlar, sanalar:\n  on Monday, on Friday\n  on January 1st, on my birthday\n  on the weekend (AmE) / at the weekend (BrE)\n\n📌 IN + oylar, yillar, fasllar, davrlar:\n  in January, in 2024\n  in summer, in winter\n  in the morning, in the evening\n  in 5 minutes (kelajakda)\n\n📌 AT + aniq vaqt:\n  at 7 AM, at noon\n  at night, at midnight\n  at the moment (hozir)\n\n🔴 Eslab qoling:\n  ON = kun (Monday)\n  IN = oy/yil/fasldavr (January/summer)\n  AT = soat (7 AM)",
    "5️⃣ 'WHEN?' — QACHON?\n\n📌 SAVOL:\n  When is your birthday? — Tug'ilgan kuningiz qachon?\n  When do you work? — Siz qachon ishlaysiz?\n\n📌 JAVOB:\n  My birthday is in March. — Mart oyida.\n  I work on Monday. — Dushanba kuni.\n  I study in the morning. — Ertalab.\n  I sleep at night. — Kechasi.\n\n📌 'When' + predlog:\n  When + do/did/will + subject + V...",
    "6️⃣ YIL, ASR, YILBOYI\n\n📌 Yil: in 2024, in 2025\n  I was born in 2010. (Men 2010 da tug'ilganman)\n\n📌 Asr: the 21st century (21-asr)\n  in the 21st century (21-asrda)\n\n📌 Yil boshi / oxiri:\n  at the beginning of January (yanvar boshi)\n  at the end of the year (yil oxiri)\n\n📌 'The' artikl:\n  in the morning ✅, in the afternoon ✅, in the evening ✅\n  in morning ❌, in afternoon ❌",
    "7️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• On the Monday ❌ (on Monday ✓ — the yo'q)\n• In Monday ❌ (on Monday ✓ — kun = on)\n• At January ❌ (in January ✓ — oy = in)\n• In winter — qishda ✓, in the winter — ham to'g'ri\n• I born in 2010 ❌ (I was born in 2010 ✓ — 'was' kerak)\n• When is your birth? ❌ (When is your birthday? ✓)",
