  rules: [
    "1️⃣ SOAT AYTISH\n\n📌 To'liq soat: 7:00 = seven o'clock\n  1:00 = one o'clock\n  13:00 = one o'clock (yoki thirteen hundred)\n\n📌 YARIM SOAT: 7:30 = half past seven\n  'half past' = yarim soat o'tdi\n\n📌 CHORAK:\n  7:15 = quarter past seven (chorak o'tdi)\n  7:45 = quarter to eight (sakkizga chorak bor)\n\n📌 MINUTLAR:\n  7:05 = five past seven (yoki seven oh five)\n  7:10 = ten past seven\n  7:25 = twenty-five past seven\n  7:55 = five to eight",
    "2️⃣ AM VA PM\n\n📌 AM (ante meridiem) — ertalab/tushgacha:\n  7:00 AM = ertalab 7:00\n  12:00 AM = yarim tun\n\n📌 PM (post meridiem) — tushdan keyin/kechqurun:\n  1:00 PM = tushdan keyin 1:00 (13:00)\n  12:00 PM = tush (12:00)\n\n📌 Savol:\n  Is this AM or PM? — Bu ertalabmi yoki kechqurunmi?\n\n🔴 12:00 PM = tush, 12:00 AM = yarim tun (chalkashlik!)\n  12 PM = 12:00 kunduzi\n  12 AM = 00:00 yarim tun",
    "3️⃣ PRESENT SIMPLE — 3-SHAXS QOIDASI\n\n📌 QOIDA: He/She/It + fe'l + -s/-es\n\n  I work → He works (ishlash → ishlaydi)\n  I go → She goes (borish → boradi)\n  I have → He has (ega bo'lish → ega)\n  I do → He does (qilmoq → qiladi)\n  I study → She studies (o'qish → o'qiydi)\n  I watch → He watches (tomosha → tomosha qiladi)\n\n📌 -ES qo'shish:\n  -sh, -ch, -x, -s, -z, -o → +es (goes, watches, does)\n\n📌 Y → IES:\n  study → studies\n  carry → carries\n  try → tries",
    "4️⃣ KUNLIK TARTIB (DAILY ROUTINE)\n\n📌 Ertalab:\n  I wake up at 7 AM. (Men 7 da uyg'onaman)\n  I brush my teeth. (Tishlarimni yuvaman)\n  I take a shower. (Dush qabul qilaman)\n  I have breakfast. (Nonushta qilaman)\n  I go to work/school. (Ishga/maktabga ketaman)\n\n📌 Kechqurun:\n  I come home. (Uyga qaytaman)\n  I have dinner. (Kechki ovqat yeyman)\n  I watch TV. (TV ko'raman)\n  I go to bed at 11 PM. (11 da yotaman)\n\n📌 3-shaxs (he/she):\n  He wakes up at 7. (U 7 da uyg'onadi)\n  She goes to work. (U ishga ketadi)",
    "5️⃣ 'AT + SOAT' QOIDASI\n\n📌 Soat + at:\n  at 7 AM, at 9:30, at noon\n  I start work at 9 AM.\n\n🔴 'o'clock' faqat to'liq soatda:\n  ✅ 7 o'clock, 9 o'clock\n  ❌ 7:30 o'clock (to'g'ri: half past seven)\n\n🔴 'at night', 'at noon', 'at midnight':\n  ✅ at night ❌ in the night\n  ✅ at noon ❌ in noon\n  ✅ at midnight ❌ in midnight",
    "6️⃣ KUNLIK FE'LLAR (DAILY VERBS)\n\n📌 Oddiy fe'llar:\n  wake up — uyg'onmoq\n  get up — turmoq\n  brush — tozalash (tish)\n  wash — yuvmoq\n  take a shower — dush qabul qilmoq\n  get dressed — kiyinmoq\n  have breakfast — nonushta qilmoq\n  have lunch — tushlik qilmoq\n  have dinner — kechki ovqat yeymoq\n  go to work/school — ishga/maktabga bormoq\n  come home — uyga qaytmoq\n  go to bed — yotmoq\n  sleep — uxlamoq",
    "7️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• 7:30 o'clock ❌ (half past seven ✓)\n• At 7:30 in the morning — to'g'ri ✓\n• He go to school ❌ (He goes to school ✓)\n• I am 25 age, I wake up at 7 o'clock ❌ (to'g'ri: I am 25 years old. I wake up at 7 o'clock.)\n• I go bed at 11 ❌ (I go to bed at 11 ✓)\n• She have breakfast at 8 ❌ (She has breakfast at 8 ✓)",
  ],
